The '''Vilcabamba Liberation Movement''' ({{Langx|ca|Moviment d'Alliberament de Vilcabamba}}, '''MLA'''; {{Langx|ay|Vilcabampa Qhapaq Taki}} {{Langx|qu|Vilcabampa Qullqaynin}}) is an [[W:United front|united front]] of [[Kawsani people|Kawsani]]-[[Jachani people|Jachani]] {{W|political organization|political}} and militant organizations founded on 27 April 1988. At its height in 1993, the MLV numbered about 100,000 members and associates. The group emerged from various {{W|indigenismo|indigenist}} organizations, establishing their base of support among the rural Indigenous communities across the territory during the [[internal conflict in Potocsí]]. 

The MLV was created with the goal of the the establishment of an independent [[Free Territory of Vilcabamba]], with some calling for the complete overthrow of the [[Potocsí|Potocsino]] state, which they consider to be an illegitimate remnant of Illypnian [[W:Imperialism|imperialism]] and {{W|settler colonialism}} in [[Abyala]]. 

